## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data ingestion setup with common AWS services and security considerations.

## Key Concepts
- JSON flattening, Parquet storage, hourly partitions
- Glue Crawlers, Glue ETL (Python), Catalog with Lake Formation
- KMS encryption, IAM least privilege, data quality checks

## Code Example
```python
# flatten nested json
import json

def flatten(record):
    flat = {}
    for k, v in record.items():
        if isinstance(v, dict):
            for kk, vv in v.items():
                flat[f"{k}_{kk}"] = vv
        else:
            flat[k] = v
    return flat
```

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses multi-source schema drift and basic data unification, a common beginner challenge.

## Key Concepts
- Schema unification across sources
- Type coercion rules and compatibility
- Parquet partitioning and Glue Catalog
- Simple schema versioning and data quality checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: unify two schemas into canonical and write Parquet
function merge(a,b){
  const canon = {};
  // map fields, coerce types
  canon.id = toIntOrNull(a.id||b.id);
  canon.name = a.name||b.name;
  // nested fields example
  canon.meta = a.meta ?? b.meta ?? {};
  return canon;
}
```

